# Personal Security Audit — Day 1

## Security Posture Summary

Assessment identified no known breaches for the primary email, but
several account-security weaknesses were found. The primary risks
were 2FA being disabled on key accounts, password reuse, and
approximately 5 accounts potentially having email-based password
recovery paths. Remediation completed included enabling 2FA and
changing the primary email password; remaining items require
follow-up.

## Actions Taken During Audit

- [x] Enabled 2FA on primary email
- [x] Changed primary email password
- [x] Checked email for known breaches using Have I Been Pwned
- [x] Reviewed services associated with the email using Epieos
- [x] Identified accounts requiring further password-recovery review

